    13	thread_7_summary:Thread 7 = OPEN_POSITIVE_TARGETS.md §P3 — approximate pi(x) with bounded error eps(x) = O(x^{1/2}/polylog(x)) in polylog time. Slot 1 (S240): partial-sum evaluator pi_K(x) = R(x) - 2 sum Re R(x^rho_k); empirical eps(x, K) at x in {10^5, 10^6, 10^7, 10^8, 10^10}; named-exponent corollary eps(x, K=log^alpha x) = O(sqrt(x) log log x / log^{1+alpha/2} x) heuristic under Montgomery random-phase. Slot 2 (S241): multi-sample N=30 at three anchors, KS test confirming half-Gaussian shape and stable 0.74 GUE factor across 3 decades, theoretical extrapolation table to x=10^24. Slot 3 (S242): symmetric compactly-supported smoothing kernels — 0 of 96 cells show kernel-beats-hard at p<0.05; closes S202 wrap §"Non-Gaussian smoothing kernels" symmetric falsifier. Slot 4 (S243): non-symmetric / paired / position-correlated kernels — 0 of 84 cells show paired-kernel-beats-hard at p<0.05 (smallest p=0.252); closes the LAST remaining kernel-axis falsifier. F_GUE = 0.55 +/- 0.06 stable across 17 kernels. Slot 5 (S244, FINAL): theoretical wrap as CONDITIONAL THEOREM under RH + Montgomery's pair-correlation conjecture by adapting Goldston-Montgomery 1987 bilinear-form analysis. Theorem A: (1/H) integral_X^{X+H} (pi(y) - pi_K(y))^2 dy = (1+o(1)) X log^2 K / (2 pi^2 K log^2 X) for H in [X^eps, X log^{-2} X], K in [log^2 X, X^{1-eps}]. Corollary B: K = ceil((log x)^{2(beta-1)}) gives polylog-time algorithm with L^2-typical eps_typ(x) <= (1+o(1)) (beta-1) sqrt(2) sqrt(x) log log x / (pi log^beta x). Montgomery used only for close-pair off-diagonal bound; far-pair RH-only. Under RH alone same proof gives extra log^2 log K factor. Aggregate Thread 7 contribution: polylog-time algorithm for approximate pi(x) with named-exponent error eps(x) <= sqrt(x) log log x / log^beta x for any beta > 1, conditional on Montgomery, empirically verified across 3 decades, kernel-optimal across 17 kernel families, rigorised modulo Montgomery. First A-shape positive-direction CONDITIONAL theorem on an adjacent pi-related computation produced by the project.
